# mksquashfs -ef excludes (live-build passes -wildcards, so entries must be
# paths RELATIVE to the squashfs root: a leading / is a FATAL ERROR:
#   "FATAL ERROR: /, ./ and ../ prefixed excludes not supported with
#    -wildcards or -regex options"
# That cost a full build (#36) before test/stages/stage-a.sh learned to check
# it. Do not add a leading slash here.
#
# Everything a *build* needs but a *booted image* must not carry.
#
# var/cache/klh-pool

# live-build installs squashfs-tools INSIDE the chroot when it builds the
# squashfs, i.e. AFTER every chroot hook — so apt rebuilds its binary caches
# and the command-not-found apt hook rebuilds its DB, no matter what
# zzz-klh-nondeterminism.hook.chroot deletes. Those four files then carry
# build-time state into an otherwise reproducible image (measured: they were
# the only genuinely non-deterministic content left in builds #36/#37).
# Excluding them here is the same thing as deleting them, but it cannot be
# undone by a later stage. All four are pure caches and regenerate on use.
var/cache/apt/pkgcache.bin
var/cache/apt/srcpkgcache.bin
var/lib/command-not-found/commands.db
var/lib/command-not-found/commands.db.metadata is filled by zzz-klh-deb-pool.hook.chroot (~900MB of the
# build's own .deb files) so the host can harvest them into the
# content-addressed pool after the build. Shipping it would nearly double the
# ISO; it exists only between the chroot hook and build.sh's harvest step.
var/cache/klh-pool
